    "result_text": "The build passes with the single acceptance test suite green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct membership-level rules with a points system, keeping logic where it belongs.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`):\n- Added `getMembershipPoints()` \u2014 starts at 0 and adds: `+2` email present, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` household of 3+, `+3` tenure over 365 days. Each rule is expressed via a named constant and a small predicate.\n- Reworked `getMembershipLevel()` to derive purely from `getMembershipPoints()`: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+) \u2014 reusing the points method rather than recomputing factors.\n- Added a small `hasLargeHousehold()` helper (household size \u2265 3) alongside the existing `hasEmail()`/`hasQualifyingTenure()` helpers, so each factor stays a single-responsibility unit.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`):\n- Added the `membershipPoints` schema field and updated the `membershipLevel` description to reflect the derived mapping. The generated `OwnerDto` picks up the new field and MapStruct wires it from `getMembershipPoints()` by name, so both fields are returned.\n\nThe acceptance test (`membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2` for a fresh owner with an email and no namesake) passes, and the build is green.",
