    "probe_recall": 0.4146341463414634,
    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The chain runs: framework validation \u2192 controller body (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2192 service (`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`) \u2192 persistence. Notably, there are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist`, entity listeners) or published events \u2014 every derived field and check is explicit in the code.\n\n## Framework layer (before controller body)\n\n1. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`) \u2014 fails fast with 400:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/`'`/`-`-separated parts)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email` (optional/nullable)\n   - `postcode`, `registrationDate`, `birthDate`, `sharesHousehold` \u2014 no bean-validation constraints\n2. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (enforced only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; inert when security is disabled).\n\n## Controller body (`addOwner`)\n\n3. **Address normalization** (side-effect, mutates DTO) \u2014 `addressNormalizer.normalize`: trims, collapses whitespace, uppercases, expands ST/RD/AVE.\n4. **Field presence validation** \u2014 `ownerFieldsValidator.validate`: rejects blank/whitespace-only firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n5. **Postcode validation** \u2014 `postcodeValidator.validate(postcode, city)`: if postcode present, must be 4 digits within the city's region range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n6. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n7. **Telephone normalization** (side-effect) \u2014 `telephoneNormalizer.normalize` \u2192 E.164; invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n8. **Email normalization** (side-effect) \u2014 `emailNormalizer.normalize`: blank\u2192null; else syntax check (`InvalidEmailException`), lowercase, disposable-domain blocklist (`DisposableEmailDomainException`).\n9. **Future registration-date guard** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is after server date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n10. **Business-day resolution** (side-effect) \u2014 effective date (registrationDate or today) rolled weekend\u2192Monday via `businessDayResolver.toBusinessDay`, stored back on `registrationDate`.\n11. **Daily registration limit** \u2014 `countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate) >= 100` \u2192 `OwnerDailyRegistrationLimitExceededException`.\n12. **Bulk-signup warning flag** (side-effect) \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = (count > 80)`.\n13. **City capacity limit** \u2014 `countOwnersInCity(city) >= 50` \u2192 `OwnerCityCapacityExceededException`.\n14. **Household ID assignment** (side-effect) \u2014 if postcode present, sets `householdId = householdIdGenerator.generate(lastName, postcode)` (SHA-256 prefix).\n15. **Duplicate identity check** \u2014 `findOwnersByIdentityKey(identityKey)` non-empty \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (identityKey = `telephone|email|householdId`).\n16. **Duplicate household check** \u2014 `findHouseholdDuplicateOf(owner)` non-null AND `sharesHousehold != true` \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException`.\n\n## Service layer (`saveOwner`, `@Transactional`)\n\n17. For a new owner, sets these derived fields in order (each only if not already set):\n    - `customerCode` = region + SHA-256 hash of telephone+lastName\n    - `namesakeCount` = count of owners with same first+last name\n    - `membershipNumber` = `customerCode-M<yy>` from registration year\n    - `householdSize` = count of same-household owners + 1\n18. **Persist** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.\n\n## After save\n\n19. **Audit log** (side-effect) \u2014 `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` writes an INFO line to the `AUDIT` SLF4J logger.\n20. Map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n**One correctness caveat worth flagging:** the duplicate/limit checks in steps 11, 13, 15, and 16 each call `ownerRepository.findAll()` and filter in memory, with no backing unique DB constraint. They're read-then-write without locking, so under concurrent requests they're racy \u2014 two simultaneous creates can both pass the same check."
